  "text": "France’s early changes—Kolo Muani for Dembélé and Thuram for Giroud—helped steady the game rather than immediately create chances. Their pass share rose from 30% before the changes to 53.9% afterward, but they still registered 0 shots in that following window. [[ev:sb:3869685:1378]] [[ev:sb:3869685:1379]] After Acuña replaced Di María, Argentina’s attacking outlet faded: their next window produced 0 shots, while France managed 2. French pressure was already building, so the substitution alone cannot explain that shift. [[ev:sb:3869685:2355]] [[ev:sb:3869685:2517]]\n\nThe clearest change in threat followed Camavinga and Coman’s introductions: France went from 0.128 xG in the preceding window to 0.897 afterward, despite having less pass share. [[ev:sb:3869685:2660]] [[ev:sb:3869685:2661]] Mbappé’s penalty and equaliser turned that threat into goals. **The key shift was from territorial pressure to decisive chances**, not simply more possession. These are unequal-length windows and associations, not proof the substitutions caused the comeback. [[ev:sb:3869685:2928]] [[ev:sb:3869685:2987]]",
